@node Listing Issues
@section Listing Issues
@cindex listing issues

@deffn Command beads-list-all
List all issues in a @code{beads-list-mode} buffer, closed ones included,
honouring @code{beads-list-default-limit}.  From the dispatch menu press
@kbd{l}; the command runs immediately.  With a status filter already set
by the filter transient it lists exactly that status.
@end deffn

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-list-issues (&key directory spec)
Display issues matching SPEC in the list buffer, programmatically.  This is
the entry point for consumer packages; it is a function, not an
interactive command.
@end deftypefn

@deffn Command beads-list-filter-menu
Refine the current list.  In a list buffer press @kbd{/}.  Toggle
@kbd{s} status, @kbd{t} type, @kbd{p} priority, @kbd{a} assignee, and
@kbd{l} label; @kbd{r} limits to ready issues, @kbd{A} includes closed
issues, @kbd{n} sets a limit, and @kbd{o} sets the order.  @kbd{RET}
applies the resulting spec and refreshes the buffer; @kbd{R} resets the
controls.
@end deffn

@deffn Command beads-list-filters
Open the curated switch-based list transient (@kbd{M-x
beads-list-filters}).  The dispatch menu's @kbd{l} lists all issues
directly instead.  Its filters are @kbd{-s} status, @kbd{-t} type,
@kbd{-p} priority, @kbd{-a} assignee, and @kbd{-l} label; its options are
@kbd{-o} order, @kbd{-n} limit, and @kbd{-r} ready only.  Press @kbd{l}
for all issues, @kbd{r} for ready, @kbd{b} for blocked, or @kbd{c} for
closed to run the list and refresh the buffer.
@end deffn

@table @kbd
@kindex r
@item r
List ready (unblocked) issues.
@kindex b
@item b
List blocked issues.
@kindex /
@item /
In a list buffer, open the spec-based filter menu to refine the current
view (@pxref{Listing Issues}).
@end table

@deffn Command beads-list-advanced
Open the full-featured list transient with every @command{bd list} flag.
Its basic filters use @kbd{-s} status, @kbd{-P} priority, @kbd{-T} type,
and @kbd{-a} assignee; @kbd{C-x l} reveals the text, date, and output
groups.  Press @kbd{x} to list with the chosen filters, or @kbd{R} to reset
them.
@end deffn

@deffn Command beads-ready
List ready (unblocked) issues for the current store.
@end deffn

@deffn Command beads-blocked
List blocked issues for the current store.
@end deffn

