* Sorting Pagination and Movement::
@end menu

@node Sorting Pagination and Movement
@subsection Sorting, Pagination, and Movement
@cindex sorting
@cindex pagination

@table @kbd
@kindex S
@item S
Sort the list.  A grouped list prompts @code{Sort by:} for a column (ID,
Type, Status, Priority, Agents, Title, Created, or Updated), defaults to the
current sort column, and toggles the direction when you pick the same column
again.  A flat list sorts by the column under point.
@kindex ]
@item ]
Move to the next page.
@kindex [
@item [
Move to the previous page.
@kindex G
@item G
Jump to a page.
@end table

@vindex beads-list-default-limit
The number of rows shown by default is the user option
@code{beads-list-default-limit}.

@cindex page size
@cindex server-side pagination
Each page holds the rows that fit the window (with a floor of five).
On a proxied-server store the list fetches that page from @code{bd} with
@code{--limit} and @code{--offset}; on an embedded or direct store it
fetches the bounded result once and slices it in Emacs.  The pager never
asks for a total, so @kbd{]} stops at the first short page.  Because
offset paging is not snapshot-safe, a row repeated by an insert between
fetches is dropped and @kbd{g} reloads from page 1.

@kbd{TAB} and @kbd{S-TAB} move between rows and wrap; @kbd{SPC} previews
the issue at point in another window (@pxref{One Movement Scheme}).

