@node Editing Issues
@section Editing Issues
@cindex editing issues

@table @kbd
@kindex E
@item E
Edit the description in a compose buffer.
@kindex N
@item N
Add a comment in a compose buffer.
@kindex e
@item e
Edit a field inline (a single-line title, or a temporary buffer for
longer fields).
@end table

From a show buffer, @kbd{?} opens the shared dispatch menu
(@pxref{Transients}).  For a compact, stay-open menu of actions for the
issue at point, run @kbd{M-x beads-show-actions}: each suffix keeps that
menu open, so you can run several without reopening it.

@node Closing and Reopening
@section Closing and Reopening
@cindex closing issues
@cindex reopening issues

@deffn Command beads-actions-close
@kindex d
Close the issue at point.  @command{bd} requires a reason, so you are
prompted for one.  When marks are active it closes every marked issue
with the same reason.
@end deffn

@deffn Command beads-actions-reopen
@kindex o
Reopen a closed issue, prompting for an optional reason.  In
@code{beads-show-mode} reopen lives in the actions transient because
@kbd{o} follows references in another window.
@end deffn

@node Claiming Status and Priority
@section Claiming, Status, and Priority
@cindex claiming
@cindex status
@cindex priority

@table @kbd
@kindex C
@item C
Claim the issue at point.  This runs immediately; the current actor is
assigned.
@kindex s
@item s
Set status (@code{open}, @code{in_progress}, @code{blocked}, @dots{}).
@kindex #
@item #
Set priority, from @code{0 - Critical} through @code{4 - Backlog}.
@end table

All three honour marks in list mode.

@node Dependencies
@section Dependencies
@cindex dependencies

@deffn Command beads-dep
Open the dependency menu: add, remove, list, and inspect the dependency
graph for an issue.
@end deffn

Press @kbd{d} from the dispatch menu for the dependency menu.

@table @kbd
@kindex a
@item a
Add a dependency (source depends on target, plus type).
@kindex r
@item r
Remove a dependency.
@kindex l
@item l
List dependencies for an issue.
@kindex t
@item t
Show the full dependency tree, walking transitively.
@kindex c
@item c
Check the project for dependency cycles.
@kindex R
@item R
Create a bidirectional @code{relates_to} link.
@kindex U
@item U
Remove a @code{relates_to} link.
@end table

@node Labels
@section Labels
@cindex labels

@deffn Command beads-label-menu
Open the label menu: add, remove, propagate, and list labels.  Press
@kbd{L} from the dispatch menu, or run @kbd{M-x beads-label-menu} (@code{beads-label}
is the non-interactive function behind it).
@end deffn

@table @kbd
@kindex a
@item a
Add a label to one or more issues.
@kindex r
@item r
Remove a label from one or more issues.
@kindex p
@item p
Propagate a label to all children of an issue.
@kindex l
@item l
List labels for a specific issue.
@kindex L
@item L
List all labels in the store.
@end table

@node Bulk Actions
@section Bulk Actions
@cindex bulk actions

Mark issues in a list buffer (@kbd{m}), then use a context action such as
@kbd{d}, @kbd{o}, @kbd{s}, or @kbd{#} to apply it to every marked issue.
The @kbd{B} prefix adds dedicated bulk commands (@kbd{B s}, @kbd{B p},
@kbd{B c}, @kbd{B o}).
